course: dictionary
lesson: 15151
title: Compound words: schoolfriend
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A schoolfriend is a friend you know from school, especially someone in your class or year. «Mia invited six schoolfriends to her birthday party.» The schoolfriends are the children Mia knows from school.
explain: Look at the word: school and friend joined together make schoolfriend. Words joined like this are called compound words. When you meet a long word, look for two smaller words inside it, because they often give you its meaning.
explain: Adults use the word too, but for a different time. «Dad bumped into an old schoolfriend at the shops» means a friend from when Dad was at school, many years ago. The word stays the same; only the time you knew them changes.
fact: A schoolfriend is a friend you know from school.
fact: Schoolfriend is a compound word: school + friend.
fact: The plural of schoolfriend is schoolfriends: more than one schoolfriend.
fact: «Old schoolfriend» means a friend from your schooldays, a phrase adults often use.
fact: Schoolfriend is a noun, a word for a person.
exercise: «Mia invited six schoolfriends to her party.» Who are the schoolfriends? | Her cousins from the farm | *Friends Mia knows from school | Strangers she met on holiday | Her teachers
exercise: «Mia invites 8 schoolfriends; each gets 3 balloons.» How many balloons are there in total? | 11 | *24 | 30 | 16
exercise: Which two smaller words are joined to make schoolfriend? | school and end | scho and olfriend | *school and friend | tool and friend
test: «Dad met an old schoolfriend at the park.» What does old schoolfriend mean here? | *A friend from Dad's schooldays | A new neighbour | A teacher who has retired | A shopkeeper
test: Which word is the plural of schoolfriend? | school-friend | schoolfriendy | friendschool | *schoolfriends
exam: Which sentence uses schoolfriend correctly? | I schoolfriend the bus to town every morning. | Schoolfriend the sun shone brightly over the hill. | The kitten was my schoolfriend, and it purred all day. | *We played football with our schoolfriends at break time.
